I remember both, and still have mine. I did an "unsupported" install,
putting my Robin inside the VT103! The 103 connector originally designed to
take the 105/125 graphics option is compatable with the Robin connector as
well. The only problems were (1) The #!%@ "fix" board on the robin wouldn't
clear the smaller spacing. I fixed that by removing the board, removing the
socket from the robin board and soldering it to the back side, then removing
the plug from the "fix" board and sildering it to the front. The fix then
plugged in from the back instad if the front; and (2) the back needed new
holes which were easilly created with a Dremel MotoTool. Complete
installation was quicker than putting a Robin into a VT100 because I didn't
have to install the cage & backplane.

I finally tired of the Robin, and deinstalled it from the VT103. Both reside
in the basement of the "Kaplow Computer Museum" along with one of my PDTs
and the remaining parts of my H-11. 

