Hi everybody,

I would like to post a problem that we have encountered in our talks with one
of our customers.
This customer has various platforms with different applications running on
them. These platforms include AS400, WANG, Novell, BULL and MVS. There are a
few more. He would like to access these applications/platforms from _one_
user-interface. So data from the MVS-application are displayed in the same
screen-layout as the the data from the other applications.

We thought of two possible solutions:

1. Develop a presentation-layer on a PC under Windows using OLE.
2. Develop a presentation-layer on UNIX with a connection/communication
   program to the different emulation-software packages.

Is there anyone that has encountered a similar problem (there must be ...)
and what did you do to solve it?

Could you please send your (possible) solutions/remarks to my e-mail address,
because we do not have general access to the newsgroups that this message
was posted to.


