   re: my previous post

   So much for my math ability.  The Quad 2100 2/275 is good for 2.2
   billion instructions per second (4 processors * 2 decode units each
   * 275 million cycles per second), the uniprocessor version is good
   for slightly over a half-billion instructions per second.

   The next generation DECchip 21164 is good for 1.2 billion at 300 MHz.
   (1 processor * 4 decode units each * 300 million cycles per second).

   And MIPS and MHz-based comparisions are, again, meaningful only when
   one factors in the differences in the instruction sets.

