> fixed 8192-byte size (assuming that is the problem)?

That is indeed the problem; one solution is FIX_SAVESET, a public-domain
program that converts ftp-transferred save sets to a format VMS BACKUP
accepts.  I couldn't find it on any ftp site (does anyone know of a site that
archives it?), so if you'd like I can email it to you.

> I've been told there may be public domain that will run on the Sun and
> restore the save set to a normal looking directory hierarchy.

That's vmsbackup, available from various ftp sites.  It works well for many
users, but it doesn't perform error detection or correction, and under some
circumstances can silently garble your data.  If you use it, I recommend
manually verifying the files it restores.

An alternative that correctly handles VMS BACKUP error detection/correction
mechanisms is Boston Business Computing's Vbackup.  For more information, you
can send email to sales@bbc.com.

