>Paul B. Denning (pauld@mbunix.mitre.org) wrote:
>> I have ftp'd the save set from the Sun to the Vax
>> (using binary mode), but I haven't been able to get the backup command to
>> work (VMS 5.5).

>> Is there a way to copy from a fixed 512-byte record size to a
>> fixed 8192-byte size (assuming that is the problem)?

>That is indeed the problem; one solution is FIX_SAVESET, a public-domain
>program that converts ftp-transferred save sets to a format VMS BACKUP
>accepts.  I couldn't find it on any ftp site (does anyone know of a site that
>archives it?), so if you'd like I can email it to you.

The following works for me (under VMS 6.1):

$! FIX_BACKUP.COM, by Keith Lewis
$ set file 'p1' /ATTR=LRL=32256

That is for backup savesets created on a disk, where the default block size
is 32256 bytes.  You may need to change it to LRL=8192 for tape savesets.

