> My mail directory is exported from a Solaris2.4 SUN.
> My DECstation running Ultrix4.3 doesn't recognize the contents
> of the mailfile, if it's written by Solaris2.4 sendmail.
> 
> The difference between a mailfile from Ultrix-sendmail and
> Solaris2-sendmail ist the first line of each mail. The date
> contains no seconds under Solaris. But Ultrix /usr/ucb/mail needs
> them to see the start of a new mail.

That's not the only difference.  The Solaris /bin/mail doesn't escape
"From " lines that appear in the message body.  Instead, it adds a
nonstandard Content-Length header to each message that's supposed to
give the length of the message body.

> Where can I get a substitute for /usr/ucb/mail that is able to read
> Solaris mailfiles?

I recommend installing BSD's mail.local for mail delivery on the
Solaris machine.  It generates mail files which are compatible with
what other systems use.

