John van de Vegte <vegte@cs.utwente.nl> writes:
>I resently bought a 2nd handed DSP3105S hard drive, whin no 
>additional data on it.
>
>Can somebody help me on the specs and/or configuration (jumpers,etc) ?

It is essentially a DEC RZ26 drive.
The jumpers are L to R

ID0,1,2 - SCSI ID
Fault - Tracks fault lite
Busy - Tracks busy lite
+5.0
SPIN-UP - Spins up on PU if installed...
AC Low
reserved
Spindle_sync
The board jumpers are the SCSI term. source jumpers

Capacity is 1.005 GB with 14 tracks, 2570 cyl. and 57 sectors.

I might comment that the drive is a bit loud and runs REAL hot, so make sure
you have good air circulation around it.

