We're running an antique 3000 model 400 for our Internet server at a
meager 133 MHz.  Our systems administrator comes from the Sun camp and
says that it matches the SPARCstation 20/61 that he's used to working on,
two years newer.  He loves the strength of the OS, and I'm a fan of the
AdvFS, which makes fsck's a thing of the past -- important when you're
providing services to paying customers, cause when you do go down, you're
back up in a heartbeat.  The AdvFS (which comes with the system out of the
box) provides for much larger file systems than standard U*X systems,
on-line backups, file striping, trashcans, load balancing, and on-line
volume modifications and additions to match the hot-swap of the
StorageWorks rack in the 2100.

We're currently running gn which is a combined httpd and gopherd, but
we'll be migrating in the next few weeks to just a pure Web server.  We do
POP, DNS, and are ready to do news when necessary.

According to this week's InfoWorld, you can also expect an upgrade to the
21164 in that box next month.  Four of those processors should keep you
happy for a long time to come.

