As far as I can remember, it's the bottom twenty pins on the bottom 
backplane connector block. Only about four of the pins on the 20-pin
connector are used, and they're all near the bottom end of the
connector.
The baud rate is determined by a set of four jumper plugs on the same 
backplane connector. Usually, a table of jumper positions and baud
rates
is stuck to the card-cage rear cover. 

