In article <9503241401.AA37661@spoelhof.sponge>, spoelhof@kodak.com (Gordon Spoelhof) writes:
> Rec Len?    ???   (Printer?) text         Padding
>----------- ----- ----------------------- ---------
>30 30 31 34 03 8D 61 61 61 61 61 61 61 61 5E ....  <end of block>

Take a look at the I/O User's Guide, the chapter on the terminal driver, the
section on "Write Function Carriage Control".  

I believe that this would be the prefix and postfix carriage control for a
print line.  '03' would mean to skip 3 lines, print the print line, then '8D'
is interpreted as "bit 7=1, so interpret bits 0-4 as an ASCII control character
[0D = Carriage Return]".  

So, '03 8D' says to "skip 3 lines, print the line, then print a <cr>".

Then again, it might mean something else.  But, this one instance isn't
sufficient to test my theory.

