I have had quote a bit of success at attaching third part 4mm DAT drives to 
a MicroVAX 3100/20.  Primarilly I have been using Archive mechanisms.  Some
things to watch out for:

   1) The MicroVAX 3100/20 has (if I am correct) a SCSI controller FCO which
      made it a bit more standard.  This, I believe, happened about three or
      four years ago.

   2) Typically, most 4mm DAT's have a switch bank on the drive itself with
      two very important switches you will need: SCSI 1/2 and Parity Y/N.
      For the MicroVAX 3100/20 I have had all of my success with SCSI = 1
      and Parity = N (disabled).  I am not quite sure if the Parity change
      was necessary, but the SCSI 1/2 was.

Newer 4mm's like the 10GB mechanism from Archive DO NOT have a SCSI 1/2 switch.
They only work for pure SCSI 2 controllers (of which the MicroVAX 3100/20 
does not behave well with SCSI 2 tapes or disks, unless you can set them to
SCSI 1).

If you have any problems, give me a hollar.



