In article <D5LHxo.I5I@swcp.com>, phdewi@swcp.com (Phillip Williams) writes:
:Hello
:I have a uVax in a BA123 with the following boards
:M7606 slot 1
:memory in slots 2 and 3
:M7504 top
:cont board bottom
:M7957 DZv11 slot 5
:M8053 DMV11 slot 6
:M3104 DHV11 slot 7
:M7546 Tk50 
:the problem is when I try tell sysgen to go find those boards it does
:nothing. What am I doing wrong.
:phillip

    I assume the "cont board" is the M9047 DMA grant card, and if so,
    it should not be located in the bottom of slot 4 -- that's a CD
    slot in the BA123 box, and the M9047 module can be installed only
    in a Q22 slot.  BA23 slots 1 through 3 are Q22/CD; BA123 slots 1
    through 4 are Q22/CD.  (This may have fried something else in the
    system.)  It's also not clear from your note if the TQK50 is in
    the bottom of slot 8. If the TQK50 controller is in the upper part
    of slot 8, a M9047 DMA grant card will need to be in the bottom of
    slot 8.  (The BA123 Q22 serpentine pattern starts at slot 5 top, to
    slot 5 bottom, to slot 6 bottom, to slot 6T, 7T, 7B, 8B, 8T, etc.)

    You'll also want to indicate where the countdown ends -- this is
    displayed on the LEDs on the KA630 and on the digit on the KA630
    bulkhead.  (This will be useful to know should the KA630 and/or
    the memory module(s) end up being fried.)

    I'm assuming the M7957 DZV11, M8053 DMV11 and M3104 DHV11 are all
    quad-width modules.  (I *think* they are.)  If any of these modules
    are *not* quad-width, you'll need to install M9047 grant cards or
    dual-width modules next to each dual-width module...

