  It's not clear to me from your posting if the device is not physically
  installed in (or attached to) the system, or if the device driver has
  not been included in the VMUNIX kernel.  In either case, getting to the
  console prompt will not help.

  If it is the former, you will have to attach the device, or get the
  reseller to do this.  If the latter, you will probably need to
  regenerate the VMUNIX kernel.  (There may be an easier way to get
  the device support included into the kernel -- it's been a while since
  I've used makedev, and that was under ULTRIX.)  Regenerating the kernel
  means you'll need the OSF system manager's manual.

  I don't have an AlphaServer 1000 manual handy to check how to halt
  the system, but there's usually either a halt button on the system
  enclosure (often with a circle-triangle icon), or one can often press
  the <BREAK> on the console terminal.  If you got an AlphaServer 1000
  manual with the system, please check there.

