Michael Richichi (richichi@pilot.njin.net) wrote:

: And then, I was running fine for a few days, but after a few hours of the 
: monitor being on, the picture "wiggled" for a few seconds, and then enlarged
: on the screen.  It now looks like it's trying to write to a 25" monitor on

Open up the monitor and reseat the "Molex" type connectors on the circuit
boards.  First, remove the plastic shell on the back.  There is an aluminum
perforated door on the side.  Remove the screws and carefully swing the
door open.  there is a circuit board attached to the inside of the door,
with many wires going to different places.  Wiggle each connector off,
and then push it back on securely.  this should clear up the problem for
one to two years.  The connectors are tin-lead to tin-lead, and oxide
builds up, making a bad connection.  if left unfixed, the connectors
actually burn up.


