: I just inherited a Vaxstation II and know very little about this beast.

: can this actually be used as it is? A friend of mine mentioned something
: about "passcodes" from Dec?

If you want to use VMS version 5.0 or newer, you need to have PAK's
(Product authorization Keys) which contain text and numbers which permit
various software packages to run.  VMS 4.7 and earlier did not use such
a feature.  Of course, you are supposed to license all DEC software from
DEC.  If the OS is still in the machine, then the PAK's are probably
still there, too.  They may expire, however, at some time in the future.

: I need a monitor can I use a PC monitor?

A Multi-sync monitor with the capability to accept composite sync-on-green
and 50-60 KHz horizontal sweep will work fine.


