Phillip Williams (phdewi@swcp.com) wrote:
: I have a uVax in a BA123 with the following boards
: M7606 slot 1
: memory in slots 2 and 3
: M7504 top
: cont board bottom
: M7957 DZv11 slot 5
: M8053 DMV11 slot 6
: M3104 DHV11 slot 7
: M7546 Tk50 
: the problem is when I try tell sysgen to go find those boards it does
: nothing. What am I doing wrong.

M7504 is a DEQNA, which is obsolete.  What version of VMS are you running?
What address do you have these devices set to?  If you can get VMS up,
you can use SYSGEN's configure utility to find out what addresses VMS
wants to see the devices at.  There could be a backplane problem, of course.
You can look at the Q-Bus manually in console mode.  Q-Bus addresses are
mapped to physical addresses 2000xxxx, where xxxx is the lower 13 bits
of the Q-Bus address (in hex form).  So, do the following :
>>> E/P/W 2000xxxx
to see what is at that address.  You get an error message if the address
doesn't respond.
If VMS runs, then use the SYSGEN command
  SHOW/UNIBUS
and it will list all Q-Bus addresses that respond.
Note that address 777500 is the CPU's interprocessor communication register
(a little-known feature of the KA-630).


