Looking at the 750 backplane from the rear, at slot position 6,
(where the RDM plugs in), toward the bottom third of the pins,
there should be a header with some wires plugged into the "right".
The header would be plugged into the "left" set of pins if no
RDM was present.  Directly below this header should be a set of
4 jumpers.   These determine the console baud rate.

rate     a  b  c  d
300      0  0  1  0
600      0  1  1  0
1200     1  1  1 0
2400     0  0  0  1
3600     1  0  0  1
4800     1  1  0  1
9600     1  0  1  1
19200    0  1  1  1
38400    1  1  1  1


      |__|  <-- bottom of header plug
       ..   <-- skip this pair of pins
    A  |.  B
       |.
       ..   <-- skip this pair of pins
    C  ||  D
       ||

This example has a jumper at A,C and D   or 1011
Looking at the table , this would be 9600 baud.

Hope this helps.

