I had the same problem when porting an RZ56 from a VAXStation to my Windows PC. 
The problem is that there is a bit inside the drive called SPE (spin-up 
enabled) that is turned OFF by default for RZ56 drives installed in VAX 
systems.  This is so that OpenVMS can spin up the drive when it is mounted.

This causes a problem for DOS, and it looks like for the MAC.  The solution for 
DOS is a program called RZSPINUP, that allows you to set the SPE bit on.  After 
this, the drive will spin up on powerup.  I do not know if there is an RZSPINUP 
for the MAC, but I would bet that there is.

Good luck hunting for it, at least now you know what to look for!

