In article <pnord.1145684283B@vunews.valpo.edu>, pnord@exodus.valpo.edu (Paul Nord) writes:
> Good Day!
> 
> We're looking to add another LaserJet 4M or 4M plus.
> 
> We want to support printing from Novell, Macintosh, and a variety of TCP/IP
> systems including DEC OSF/1 Alpha, DEC OpenVMS Alpha, and SunOS.  HP's
> JetDirect card does support Novell, Mac, and SunOS but claims not to support
> VMS or OSF/1.  It runs as an LPD.  Seems like it should work?  Has anyone
> made it work?

We've been trying various methods of driving a JetDirect card (on a DesignJet
650) from VMS.

Using a UCX telnet symbiont works sometimes, but the telnet protocol doubles
0xFF characters, and the plotter will get confused if this happens.  Provided
the data being sent doesn't contain 0xFF, though, this seems to work OK.
Beware that raster data embedded in HPGL/2 does use this character, though -
I'm not certain whether there are other circumstances.

The Multinet stream symbiont has a NOTELNET option which disables this
doubling, and this seems to work fine for all data that we've tried.

Newer versions of the JetDirect card (someone said that Rev A.03.03 was the
first in a thread a month or two ago) support the lpd protocol.  I've tried
using a UCX lpd symbiont, and this works nearly all the time, but seems to
fail intermittently on large drawings.  I don't know why.

A strategy which does seem to work is to use a UCX lpd symbiont to send the
file to an lpd running on an HP machine, and to have the HP send the file to
the JetDirect using HP's own driver software.

A final option is to write a program which connects a socket directly to port
9100 at the JetDirect's IP address, and to simply write the data to the
socket.  This seems to work OK.

If anyone can add anything to this, and especially if they can tell me why
using an lpd symbiont directly to JetDirect cards doesn't always work, I'd
be grateful for the information.  (A copy via e-mail would be appreciated
in case I miss it on the newsgroup).
                               
Cheers,
John Aldridge
