> Has anyone else notice a significant decline in Dec's service in recent
> months?  We have had nothing with problems with our local group
> and we have never had problems in the past.

Digital Canada is separate from Digital USA, but our service organization is
superb.  Although they have cut back on management staff over the last few
years (we're on 3rd service manager in less than 5 years), the support to us
has not suffered in any way.

> Can't get spare parts to replace our dec products when they go out...

I believe that there will always be occasions when this happens, but it should
be rare.  The local office may not have the parts in stock, but they should be
able to get them quickly.  If you feel that a part is critical, then you should
be able to convince the local office that the part is worthwhile stocking or to
increase the stocking level.  Digital has guidelines as to what the stocking
requirements are compared to the equipment in your area, but I've always felt
that these were guidelines, not unbreakable rules.  The logistics manager in
your area should be willing to discuss this with you - ours certainly was.

> Closed down the local office without telling us and then we had to 
> beg someone for a number to talk to our local service manager? Then 
> he was upset with us for calling him!

If your service manager is upset when you call him, feel free to go over his
head.  Local management is there to serve *you*, not to keep his office chair
warm.  Give him a wake-up call by calling his boss, and when your service
contract comes up for renewal, issue an RFP and invite open competition. 
You'll be surprised at what Digital can do when they have to.

> Spent 4 hours on the phone with 5 different DEC people trying to get
> our DSN Link account re-activated after they goofed and shut us down.

Problems will always happen - people are human and will make mistakes.  The
strength in a service organization is in how fast they will correct those
mistakes.  I've got no complaints with our service organization on our area and
would hesitate to recommend for servicing both Digital and non-Digital
equipment (they also maintain our System Industries disk drives and CMD Hawk
storage controllers). 

Discuss your problems with your local management.  If they're not willing to
talk to you, escalate.  I suspect your problems may be local and not indicative
of a global problem.

