In article <3jlrr8$dnq@rs10.tcs.tulane.edu>, martav@rs6.tcs.tulane.edu
(Marta Martinez) writes:

>I compressed numerous files in a VMS system using the routines lzcomp
>and now I need to transfer all my files to a unix system. I have not
>been able to find any routine in unix that successfully uncompresses my
>files ....

LZCOMP has a switch that specifies UNIX-compress-compatible compression.
Use that, and then be sure to transfer the compressed files from the VMS
system to the UNIX system in binary mode.  If you didn't use that switch in
the first place, no routine you'll find on UNIX will decompress the files --
they're VMS-specific.

