John M. Collinson (jcollinson@ivory.trentu.ca) wrote:

: We are trying to find an inexpensive way to create a bridge using a 
: DECStation 2100.  Is it possible to have the DECstation 2100 use both the 
: coaxial connection and the serial connections for twisted pair ethernet at 
: the same time.  Ie in order to use it as a bridge we need to network ports. 
  
If you have an Ethernet board with a choice of media (e.g. BNC ThinWire,
AUI, and/or 10-Base-T), you can only use one such physical medium on
a given board.  

You can, however, use your ordinary serial port to run PPP to another
machine, at whatever speeds your serial hardware supports.

This will give you a low-speed bridge, at least.

