Ive got a couple of 4m+ printers that Im using with Macs, NT, and Ultrix.
To drive them from Ultrix, Im using a filter that I got off the net. This
talks to the HP printer telnet port, rather than using lpd. I tried lpd,
but I wasnt satisfied with the ammount of control that I had over the
printout (I also kept getting a trailer page out, if I forgot to do a
-h).  I actually use this filter "behind" the Ultrix ln03rof PostScript
filter. This lets me control lines & columns per page (and orientation).
The filter was actually written for something other than Ultrix, so I
would expect that it should work on OSF. 

The HP JetDirect driver was written by Lawrence LeMay
(lemay@epx.cis.umn.edu). The code is available from ftp.cs.umn.edu in the
users/lemay directory.

Here is a sample printcap entry:

#++
#  Accounting LaserJet 4m+, with JetDirect card.
#--
jgm|lp9|Accounting LaserJet 4M+:\
        :af=/usr/spool/lpd9/lp9acct:\
        :ct=dev:\
        :lp=/dev/null:\
        :lf=/usr/adm/lp9err:\
        :mc#20:\
        :mx#0:\
        :if=/usr/lib/lpdfilters/hpln03rof:\
        :pl#66:\
        :pw#132:\
        :sh:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd9:\
        :uv=4.0:\
        :xf=/usr/lib/lpdfilters/xf:

The "hpln03rof" filter shell script:

#!/bin/sh
#
# Run the print job through ln03rof and send it to a HP LaserJet with
# a JetDirect TCP/IP card.
#
# 03NOV94 JGM Original


ln03rof $* | hpdriver $* 

exit


This has been working quite well for me for several months now.


BTW, depending on the TCP/IP package you have on VMS, it may be able to
talk to the HP JetDirect directly (as it were). As I recall, TGV's
Multinet includes a symbiont to do exactly that.


Good Luck.

