In article <3ka6t2$i8n@arc.electriciti.com>, jjo@triton.com (Jay Olson) writes...
>I am looking at buying another Alpha to add to the DEC 3000/300LX which
>I have now. I was interested to see the performance specifications for the
>new AlphaStation 200 4/100. Why is it that the AlphaStation 200 4/100 with
>a 100 Mhz CPU outperforms a DEC 3000/300LX with a 125 Mhz CPU?
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=

The 300LX has a 256KB cache and 64 bit data bus into the cache. The 4/100
has a 512KB cache and a 128 bit data bus into the cache. The 4/100 also
has a faster main memory system and a faster I/O bus (33 MHz PCI vs 12.5MHz
TURBOchannel).

