We believe that we have found a bug in the DEMNA interface firmware
which causes terminal sessions to "freeze" or "hang". It is particularly
noticed using IP sessions with TGV- Multinet but also showed up in
using the LU-6 software for file transfers to an IBM machine. It first
appeared when we began to install new? Vax 6610's to replace leased 
machines. The new machines used firmware version 804 in the DEMNA
and all of the problems went away on 4 different platforms and with
2 different kinds of software when we reverted back to version 803.
We used a network sniffer to narrow the search down and a CRC error
appeared between the Vax and the first network device (multiport
transceiver). Has anyone else seen a similar problem? DEC so far
does not acknowledge any problem. Although this is our first exposure
to 804 firmware we have run DEMNA's at 803 version for some time with
no problems using the same TGV and LU-6 software.


