In article <juan_lander.12.0008CE0C@jhuapl.edu>, juan_lander@jhuapl.edu (Juan R. Lander) writes:
|>What is the difference between a TK50 and a TK70 tape drive ?

The TK70 is a later model, with cartridge capacity of 296 megabytes, compared
with 95 megabytes for the TK50. 

|>Do they used the same interface in a uVax ?

For a Q-bus MicroVAX, the TK50 uses a TQK50 controller, while the TK70 uses a
TQK70 controller.

|>Can the TK70 read TK50 tapes (Compatible) ?

Yes, the TK70 can read (but not write) TK50 tapes.

|>Do they use the same tape cartridge ?

No.  The TK70 uses a CompacTape II cartridge, the TK50 a plain CompacTape
cartridge.  You can use a CompacTape II cartridge in a TK50, but it stays at
the lower density from then on, unless you degauss it.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Keith B. Parris, StorageWorks Host-Based Software Team, Digital Equip. Corp.



