>it included in the full kit?  And if it isn't needed, why bother including it in
>the (otherwise less complete) software update kit.  I'm confused ...

The idea is that the full kit is designed to be shipped with a new
system, in such as case the ECU diskette would have been included with
the hardware rather than in the software kit. 

The software update kit, at least in theory, should only be going to
people who've previously received a full kit so only the bits that have
changed will be replaced. Take an old full kit, the hardware bundle and
the update kit, remove the superceded media and you should have exactly
what you'd get with a new hardware kit and full software kit.


