A program exists which might help solve this problem.  It's called
"screen" (possibly "GNU screen").  Its main purpose is to provide
multiple sessions on a single ACSII terminal.  Part of how it implements
that is to provide a virtual VT220 (or so) emulation.  If your
applications aren't really VT3xx-specific, they'd probably work under
screen.

I'll send a list of SCO binaries FTP sites under separate cover.  I know
a compiled "screen" is out there, but I'm not sure where, so you'll have
to search a bit.  (Try ftp.celestial.com first).  If you want to start
from source, it's somewhere out there -- try the usual UNIX sources
sites.  I don't know how difficult it would be to build.

