In article <3jdvba$onv@info-server.bbn.com>, bkort@musenet.org (Barry Kort) writes:

>I recently acquired an RRD50 CDROM drive and matching M7552 Q-Bus
>Controller for it.  I have no docs for it.
>
>Neither the MDM Customer Diagnostics TK50 nor the Ultrix 'sizer'
>program seems to recognize the presence of this card.  Nor can I
>find it among the known devices listed in /usr/field/shoadrs.

I'll assume you're using it on a MicroVAX of some flavor.  It
is supported on the MicroVAX II and the MicroVAX 3x00; x >= 5.
For shoadrs you should be looking for the controller, the KRQ50.

>
>If so, how do
>I get sizer to recognize it for the kernel configuration file?

The KRQ50 is one of the MSCP family of disk controllers.  So, it
should follow the address progression of UDA like controllers.
You need to make sure that whatever CSR address it uses doesn't
conflict with one of the existing controllers.  I don't have
the documentation for one either, so you'll still need help
finding what address the controller is using.

Once at a unique address, you can boot genvmunix as vmunix and
let doconfig (or sizer) build the appropriate configuration.  Or,
if you know how, you can just edit the configuration file to
include the new controller.  Sizer relies on genvmunix to be
able to find things.

