Michael Richichi (richichi@pilot.njin.net) wrote:

: I have come across a VAXstation 3200 with two RD54 drives and a TK50.  

Make sure the last owner didn't remove any Q-Bus boards and leave a
gap in the board sequence.  The Q-Bus machine requires continuity
from right to left, up to the last board.  If the last slot is only
partially filled, the half-height board should be on the top if it's
an even-numbered slot or on the bottom if it's an odd numbered slot.
(The interrupt chain follows a serpentine path.)

Any slot with only one board requires a Grant Continuity Card in
the vacant half.  Gaps in the Q-Bus continuity chain will prevent
bus interrupt signals from reaching any boards beyond the gap.

Barr Kort


