Bill,

  I believe the problem is in the keyboard's cable, and not the keyboard
itself.  The cable is acting like an antenna.  One thing you might try is to
go to your nearest Radio Shack store and purchase one or two "RF Snap-on
Chokes".  These worked very well for me as I have three computers in the
same room as my ham radio station, which generates much more power than your
portable radio.

  To use the chokes, unplug the keyboard cable from the terminal and wrap
the plug end of the cable inside and around the choke in a figure-8 fashion. 
If one choke doesn't solve the problem, try winding the cable around two
chokes that are snapped together .  If this still doesn't work, you might
try doing the same thing with the data cable coming into the terminal.

