MAILbus 400 - KEYpak - Interface for DEC OSF/1 AXP

Software Product Description



Product description

The MAILbus 400 - KEYpak - Interface (MKI) allows the
integration of KEYword's KEYpak converter library into the
MAILbus 400 Message Transfer Agent for the conversion of
interpersonal messaging bodyparts.

MKI supports the source and target conversion of and between
X.400 1988 bodyparts of types IA5 (text) and Externally
Defined (arbitrary document formats).



Software Requirements

-   DEC OSF/1 Operating  System
-   MAILbus 400 Message Transfer Agent for DEC OSF/1, Version
    1.2 (or later)
-   KEYpak UNIX for OSF/1 AXP, Version 3.1 (or later)



Supported IPM bodyparts

MKI processes the following bodypart types as conversion
input:

-   IA5 bodyparts
-   Externally Defined bodyparts (with the bodypart data coded
    as octet- or bitstring)

Documents of any word-processing format contained in such
bodyparts can be converted with MKI, as long as the correspon-
ding source converter of KEYpak is available and installed.

Depending on the target document format of the conversion, MKI
creates one of the following bodypart types:

-   an AI5 bodypart if the conversion is into the KEYpak af
    (Ascii File) format
-   an Externally Defined bodypart for all other target
    formats.

When creating an Externally Defined bodypart, MKI must include
an Encoded Information Type (EIT) object identifier into the
bodypart to identify the content's encoding, i.e. the format
of the document contained in the bodypart.

MKI allows to convert the source bodyparts into document
formats supported by KEYpak, as long as the corresponding
target converter of KEYpak is installed and MKI has knowledge
of the EIT for the output bodypart (or the output is an IA5
bodypart).

Over 40 of the most important target document formats of
KEYpak are currently supported as IPM bodypart targets, as
their EIT identifiers are known to MKI.

The values of the EITs for several file formats (word
processing formats, spreadsheet formats etc.) are predefined
in the NCL-scripts

-   start_mta.ncl and
-   create_mta_extdef_bodyparts.ncl

of the standard MAILbus 400 installation.

MKI has an internal table which holds the EITs defined in the
scripts above for the supported KEYpak target formats (the EIT
values used by MKI are currently based on the scripts of
MAILbus 400 Version 1.2).

If more than one EIT is defined for a document format
supported by KEYpak, the first available definition has been
taken. If a KEYpak format has no equivalent bodypart
definition in these scripts, the EIT value is unknown and this
KEYpak format is not supported as target of a bodypart
conversion, since no valid bodypart could be created by MKI.



