>DecWindows crashes when someone tries to use the DecTerm postscript file
>viewer.  The display goes black and then gives you a login prompt as a text
>terminal.

  In sys$manager:  you should find a file  DECW$SERVER_0_ERROR.LOG
  It is a verbose text file which contains entries like this
  below that  usually are NOT a problem symptom:
  4-MAR-1995 20:29:22.4 %LIB-E-ACTIMAGE, error activating image
  WSGS06$DKA300:[SYS0.SYSCOMMON.][SYSLIB]DECW$SVEXT_SHAPE.EXE;

  The last rows of that file should contain an error message that
  may be related to your problem; without this message it is
  difficult give useful hints.

  If you find a  message that looks related to virtual memory, check
  the user page-file quota, see what happens when you increase it  (
  note that quota there is another  system-wide  limit due to the
  system parameter VIRTUALPAGECNT,  that is not dynamic, so to change
  it you will have to reboot your machine).
