In early April, the DECUS membership will be receiving
a ballot in the postal mail.  Members will be asked to elect
three directors to the DECUS US Board.  In an effort to
inform the DECUS membership and interested persons about the 
candidates and their positions on issues,  Dale Coy, Terry Kennedy 
and myself, Geri Goeransson are sponsoring this candidates forum.
  

This forum is structured differently than past efforts.

Candidates, participating in this forum will be asked for
written responses to questions solicited from the membership
and interested parties.   The responses from all the candidates
will be collected and then posted for review and open to discussion.
 
All information will be posted to comp.org.decus, DECUServe, and the
Board_public Notes Conference on DCS.   

Questions will be solicited from a variety of sources.
You need not be a DECUS member to submit a question.
If you have an issue you'd like the candidates to address,
send your question to one of us:

        Dale Coy                (coy@eisner.decus.org)
        Terry Kennedy           (kennedy@eisner.decus.org)
        Geri Goeransson         (goeransson@decus.org)

The name of the person submitting the question will NOT be released
or made public.  The deadline for submitting questions is 
March 8, 1995.

Dale, Terry and I (Geri) will review the questions, picking 3-5 for
written responses.  The questions with the request for a written
response will be sent on 3/10/95 to those candidates who choose to 
participate in this forum.  Candidates will have 7-days to send their
replies to all questions by 3/17/95.  Responses from all the candidates
to the questions will be posted shortly afterwards.

Questions not used for written answers by the candidates will
be posted, electronically for discussion.

...

The success of this forum is dependent on participation.
The goal is to showcase the candidates, affording us the opportunity
to know them, their opinions, their skillset.

As a stockholder in various companies, from time to time I receive
a ballot and am asked to vote for two of the five candidates.
After reading the thumbnail biographical sketch,  I'm forced to 
make the best guess.  Based on the information provided, I don't 
always feel confident or very informed about who/what I'm voting for 
on these ballots.

So we encourage you to take advantage of this opportunity.
Submit a question(s) for the forum.
Get to know the candidates.
And as an educated voter, elect three new directors to the US DECUS Board.

Thanks for reading.
Dale Coy
Terry Kennedy
Geri Goeransson

