In article <3jht1r$2jj@lead.zk3.dec.com>, ftw@marvin.zk3.dec.com (Farrell Woods) writes:
> The machines that came with floppies that attach to the SCSI bus
> are typically 2.88 drives.  However its possible that the little
> three-position switch on the "floppy-to-SCSI- bridge controller
> is in the wrong position and thus doesn't handle the 2.88 drive
> properly.

The floppy-to-SCSI bridge uses the drive select to determine what type
of driver is attached. If drive 0 responds, it's an RX33. If drive 1
responds, it's an RX23. If drive 2 responds, it's an RX26. You're
probably thinking of the SCSI address switches...
