What type of cable did you use to connect the serial port on the board to
the serial connector. A standard PC connector cable will not work because the
majority of such cables expect a different pin layout on the board side. If you 
have used such a cable you will have to rewire your cable - check the design 
guide.

------------------------------------------------------------------
Apparently there is no standard for this. The PC world has evolved two
"standards". The majority standard has the

 2 4 6 8 x
 1 3 5 7 9

layout, which means (because the Dshell is   
  6 7 8 9
1 2 3 4 5 )

that the cable requires to be soldered, and "scrambled".

The alternative is

 6 7 8 9
 1 2 3 4 5

This is the choice on the AXPPCI33. This also allows a straight IDC cable/connectors
to be used, with no scrambling reqd.

Now to the design guide, 


Table 17 should read :

	Pin	Function	Pin	Function
	 1	DCD		 6	DSR
	 2	SIN		 7	RTS
	 3	SOUT	 	 8	CTS
	 4	DTR		 9	RI
	 5	GND		10	No pin installed


Sohail Syyed 
PS (ofcourse it might not the above problem!)


