You're correct....it has nothing to do with the license in that you can 
have an existing 5 user Novell license and a 100 user SoftNet Utilities 
license running on a DEC Alpha (or any other platform that we support) 
and everything will work fine.

Although we take advantage of the Novell administrative utilities (i.e. 
syscon, pconsole, fconsole, etc.) and client side software (i.e. 
ipx.com, netx.com, odi drivers or VLM's), we DON'T include them with our 
SoftNet Utilities Novell emulation packages because the customer already 
owns them if they have a Novell network. (They're there by default.)

It's just easier for us to say (and everyone else to understand) that 
our software allows UNIX platforms to be integrated into an EXISTING 
Novell environment. It's VERY rare that an organization would have the 
Novell administrative tools, etc. without owning a Novell network.

